From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:09:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] usb: dwc2: Keep an addressed peripheral session over
 suspend-to-idle

dwc2_suspend() disconnects the gadget (soft disconnect in L0) and powers
the PHY off, and dwc2_resume() starts a new session from a core reset.
Every suspend-to-idle therefore ends the session with the host: on the
iPad 5 the Mac enumerates the device again after each wake, USB
networking and serial reconnect, and the charger falls back to the
100 mA a new session may draw until the host grants more.

iOS never does this for sleep: IOUSBDeviceController's system power
handler takes the bus down only for power-off and restart (messages
0xe0000250 and 0xe0000310), and AppleSynopsysOTGDevice holds its PHY
power assertion from bus on to bus off.

Add params.s2idle_keep_session, set for Apple SoCs. In suspend-to-idle,
a session the host has addressed, in L0 or bus-suspended in L2, is left
as it is: the controller and PHY stay powered and connected, and both
are put on the wakeup path so that their power domains stay on. The
interrupt is off while the system sleeps, so the host sees NAKs; what it
did meanwhile (a bus resume or reset) is handled on resume as usual. If
the controller lost its state anyway, resume disconnects and reconnects
as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/core.h     | 13 +++++++
 drivers/usb/dwc2/debugfs.c  |  1 +
 drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c   |  5 +++
 drivers/usb/dwc2/platform.c | 75 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 94 insertions(+)

